(>> 6.4 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Contrast structures \(struct\) and unions \(union\) regarding memory allocation,) Tj
T*
(member accessibility, and practical use cases.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) Memory Allocation: In a struct, every member has its own separate memory) Tj
T*
(location. Total size is at least sum of member sizes plus compiler padding. In a union,) Tj
T*
(all members share SAME memory location. Size is strictly equal to size of largest) Tj
T*
(member. \(2\) Member Accessibility: In struct, all members can store distinct data) Tj
T*
(concurrently. In union, only ONE member holds meaningful data at any given instant;) Tj
T*
(writing to one member corrupts others. \(3\) Use Cases: Structures model entities with) Tj
T*
(multiple simultaneous attributes \(student records, coordinate points\). Unions used when) Tj
T*
(memory is scarce \(embedded microcontrollers\) or when an entity takes one of several) Tj
T*
(mutually exclusive formats \(variant data types, network packet headers\).) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the difference between text files and binary files in C, detailing) Tj
T*
(fread\(\) and fwrite\(\) operations.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Text files store data as human-readable ASCII or UTF-8 characters where each) Tj
T*
(line terminates with newline delimiter \('\\n' on UNIX, '\\r\\n' on Windows\). During) Tj
T*
(reading/writing, runtime performs translation. Binary files store data as raw,) Tj
T*
(unformatted byte sequences mirroring exact memory representations. Binary files require) Tj
T*
(no translation, offer higher I/O speed, and prevent rounding errors. Block I/O) Tj
T*
(functions: 'fwrite\(buffer, size, count, fp\)' writes 'count' elements of 'size' bytes) Tj
T*
(from buffer to stream; 'fread\(buffer, size, count, fp\)' reads raw bytes directly into) Tj
T*
(memory. Both return number of complete items successfully processed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 6.5 Key Takeaways and Revision Points) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Structures group diverse data; compilers add padding bytes to satisfy alignment) Tj
T*
(requirements.) Tj
T*
(* Union members share a single memory block; size equals largest member.) Tj
T*
(* Preprocessor directives \(#define, #ifdef\) execute prior to compilation; header) Tj
T*
(guards prevent multiple inclusions.) Tj
T*
(* File I/O uses stream pointers \(FILE*\); binary files use fread/fwrite; fseek enables) Tj
T*
(random access.) Tj
T*
